# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Credential-free + PII-free repo. NOTHING below may ever be committed.
#  (See docs/PRE_UPLOAD_CHECKLIST.md — start a FRESH repo, scrub first.)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# secrets / credentials
run.bat
apiKey.txt
panel.txt
secrets.json
*.key
*.pem
*.minisig
.minisign/
# scrub map with the owner's REAL SteamID/host — match at ANY depth (repo has code under src/,
# so the old root-anchored 'scripts/…' pattern missed src/scripts/scrub_targets.json). NEVER commit this.
scrub_targets.json
scripts/scrub_targets.json
src/scripts/scrub_targets.json

# runtime state / PII (SteamIDs, names, chat)
*.log
*.jsonl
ranks*.json*
match_history.json
dashboard_state.json
schedule.json
command_centre_settings.json
console_filters.json
plugin_commands.txt
plugin_ranks.txt
plugin_bans.txt
bot_overrides.json
*.done
*.bak
# 2026-07-28: the bot/web CC WRITE these into whatever folder they are run from, and running or
# importing them straight out of the checkout (a --selftest, `import no_mapvote_bot` from src/)
# drops them in src/ - where NOTHING here matched them and `git add -A` would have committed
# them. `ranks*.json*` above only matches names STARTING with "ranks", so it caught none of
# these. Files marked (PII) were verified to carry real third-party SteamIDs on a live install.
# NOTE: a '#' only starts a comment at the START of a line here - never put one after a
# pattern, it becomes part of the pattern.
# (PII) verified to carry real third-party SteamIDs on a live install:
ban_log.json
prestige.json
plugin_cfg_cache.json
# moderation reports (names + chat) and per-player counters:
plugin_reports.json
grief_flood.json
global_optin.json
# operator/runtime config the bot regenerates with defaults when absent:
rank_ladder.json
shared_ranks.json
mission_baseline.json
mission_keys.json
mission_pool.json
votemap_config.json
server_messages.json
system_messages.json
faction_colours.json
srvcfg_pending.json
# deploy markers (deployed_plugin.* is also covered further down)
deployed_*.json

# user-installed config (lives in ~/.nuke-option-toolkit, but ignore here too)
config.json

# deploy state / binaries
deployed_plugin.*
pending_plugin.*
release_out/
*.dll

# machine-generated dev dumps / harness
docs/_*.json
.claude/
AGENTS.md
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# bulk / backups / build
archive/
backups/
_server_backup/
map_backup_*/
mapdata/
# build artifacts + vendored binaries (code is under src/; match at any depth)
**/NukeStats/libs/
**/NukeStats/bin/
**/NukeStats/obj/
**/NukeStats/bepinex_pack/
**/NukeStats/bepinex_pack_win/

# un-ignore the published templates + the trusted public key
!run.bat.example
!apiKey.txt.example
!panel.txt.example
!anz.nukestats.cfg.example
!config.example.json
!installer/trusted.pub
!scripts/scrub_targets.example.json

# --- hardening (build_public_repo.py) ---
*.lnk
installer/sources.lock.json

# runtime data dirs and locks (never publish - .nost-data holds host credentials)
.nost-data/
.demo-data/
webcc.lock
